  m_Name: RotatoryVanePumpData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Rotatory Vane Pump
  engineDescription: 'A Rotary Vane Pump is a positive displacement pump used for
    transferring gases or liquids by trapping and moving fluid through rotating vanes
    inside an eccentrically mounted rotor. Its main components include the casing,
    rotor, vanes, shaft, inlet port, outlet port, end covers, and cam ring. During
    operation, the rotor rotates within the casing, causing the vanes to slide outward
    and maintain contact with the inner surface of the cam ring. This creates sealed
    chambers that expand at the inlet to draw in fluid and contract at the outlet
    to discharge it under pressure, providing smooth and continuous flow.

    Rotary
    vane pumps are widely used in vacuum systems, hydraulic systems, automotive applications,
    refrigeration units, chemical processing, and industrial fluid transfer. From
    an engineering perspective, understanding pump operation, fluid dynamics, sealing
    mechanisms, volumetric efficiency, vane motion, lubrication, wear characteristics,
    and maintenance practices is essential for ensuring reliable performance, energy
    efficiency, and long service life.'
  engineCategory: Engineering
